From: Apotheca <noreply@apotheca.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sun4i-codec: h616: the speaker off while headphones are in

The H616 codec has one analog output, LINEOUT. On Anbernic's H700
handhelds it feeds the speaker's amplifier and the headphone socket both.
The jack made for hp-det-gpios switches the "Headphone" pin only, so the
amplifier stays on with headphones in and both play, unless userland turns
"Speaker Switch" off (alsa-ucm-conf's sun4i-h616 profile does, for a sound
server; a system with none never does).

Give the jack a second pin on such a card (hp-det-gpios and an amplifier
GPIO): "Speaker", inverted. Plugged in, DAPM powers the Speaker widget
down, which takes the amplifier's GPIO low; pulled out, it comes back.
The jack's first reading, as the card is made, sets it for the start.
"Speaker Switch" still reads and sets the same pin.
---
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
@@ -1623,6 +1623,16 @@
 	{ .pin = "Headphone", .mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE },
 };
 
+/*
+ * The H616's boards have one output (LINEOUT) for the speaker's amplifier
+ * and the headphone socket both: with headphones in, the speaker goes off,
+ * and comes on again when they are out.
+ */
+static struct snd_soc_jack_pin sun50i_h616_headphone_jack_pins[] = {
+	{ .pin = "Headphone", .mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE },
+	{ .pin = "Speaker", .mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE, .invert = 1 },
+};
+
 static struct snd_soc_jack_gpio sun4i_headphone_jack_gpio = {
 	.name = "hp-det",
 	.report = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE,
@@ -1636,11 +1646,20 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	if (scodec->gpio_hp) {
+		struct snd_soc_jack_pin *pins = sun4i_headphone_jack_pins;
+		unsigned int num_pins = ARRAY_SIZE(sun4i_headphone_jack_pins);
+
+		if (scodec->gpio_pa &&
+		    of_device_is_compatible(card->dev->of_node,
+					    "allwinner,sun50i-h616-codec")) {
+			pins = sun50i_h616_headphone_jack_pins;
+			num_pins = ARRAY_SIZE(sun50i_h616_headphone_jack_pins);
+		}
+
 		ret = snd_soc_card_jack_new_pins(card, "Headphone Jack",
 						 SND_JACK_HEADPHONE,
 						 &sun4i_headphone_jack,
-						 sun4i_headphone_jack_pins,
-						 ARRAY_SIZE(sun4i_headphone_jack_pins));
+						 pins, num_pins);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(rtd->dev,
 				"Headphone jack creation failed: %d\n", ret);
